## Decide whether RAP fits

Use a RAP design when the requirement needs a transactional business object with lifecycle behavior, validations, actions, or an application service. A read-only extract may need a different shape; do not introduce a transactional model without a business reason.

## Design review points

- Identify the business object, ownership, lifecycle, and source of truth.
- Prefer released extension points and released APIs for the target product and release.
- Separate interface, projection, behavior, and service concerns according to the target platform's supported model.
- Define authorization, locking, validation, error, and draft behavior explicitly.
- Include a test plan for behavior and service exposure, not just syntax.

Confirm syntax, feature support, and release contracts in the target system. JDAP guidance is not a substitute for SAP documentation or ATC verification.
